## 🔎 Key Context Tracing & Deduplication Findings

During evaluation tracing (`llm_context_trace`), a major retrieval efficiency bottleneck was revealed:

| Question ID | Retrieved Top-K | Chunks Deduplicated | Chunks Passed to LLM | Bottleneck Cause |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :--- |
| **Q1** (Aegeon Sentence) | 10 | **6 (60%)** | 3 | Duplicate mega-parent text (`parent_text` = ~18k chars) |
| **Q2** (Mistaken Identity) | 10 | **6 (60%)** | 3 | Multiple top sub-chunks belong to identical Act section |
| **Q3** (Origin of Twins) | 10 | **6 (60%)** | 3 | Triggered hallucination filter due to bloated parent context |
| **Q4** (Arrest & Gold Chain) | 10 | **7 (70%)** | 2 | 70% of top-10 chunks dropped before prompt insertion |
| **Q5** (Climax Resolution) | 10 | **4 (40%)** | 2 | 40% dropped due to shared parent block |

> [!WARNING]
> **Primary Bottleneck**: Because `parent_text` encompasses entire Acts/Scenes (18k–22k characters), 60% to 70% of retrieved top-10 vector candidates are discarded as duplicates during hierarchical context assembly. This restricts the variety of evidence reaching the LLM to only 2 or 3 mega-blocks.

---

## 💡 Recommendations for Chunker Tuning

1. **Reduce Parent Context Scope**: Scope parent blocks to scene-level or bounded sliding windows (~2,000–3,000 chars / ~400 words) rather than full multi-page Acts.
2. **Optimize Sub-Chunk Granularity**: Target smaller, highly focused sub-chunks (~400–600 characters / ~80–100 words) with 100-character overlap for sharper embedding similarity.
3. **Refine Deduplication Logic**: Deduplicate by scene/sub-section ID rather than raw parent string matching, allowing diverse snippets across different acts to be included in the LLM prompt.
